Replace periodic-stable-jobs with local job list.

The shared periodic-stable-jobs template in openstack-zuul-jobs runs
openstack-tox-py39 on stable/2025.1, but kolla-ansible on this branch
sets python_requires >= 3.10 and requires ansible-core >= 2.17, which
itself needs Python >= 3.10. The py39 tox environment therefore cannot
even install: pip fails to resolve ansible-core in seconds, and the
job has failed on every run. In the 30 days to 2026-07-01 that was 30
failures from 30 runs in the periodic-stable pipeline, pure noise for
anyone watching the periodic dashboards.

Zuul templates cannot exclude individual jobs, so replace the shared
template with an explicit periodic-stable job list running what the
shared template would have run minus the impossible interpreter: docs
and py312. Interpreter coverage is unchanged in practice because check
already runs py310, py311 and py312 on every change proposed to this
branch. This mirrors the approach already taken for check and gate on
newer branches with the local openstack-python3-jobs-kolla-ansible
template.

